    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Compute everything",
        "body": "$12 + 34 + 56 = 102$. Then $46 + 56 = 102$, $12 + 90 = 102$, $34 + 68 = 102$, but $46 + 68 = 114$.\n\n**Answer: (D) $46+68$**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Group two of the numbers",
        "body": "$12 + 34 = 46$, so the sum is $46 + 56$ (A). $34 + 56 = 90$ gives (B), and $12 + 56 = 68$ gives (C). (D) uses 46 and 68, which double-counts the 12.\n\n**Answer: (D) $46+68$**"
      }
