    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "One prime must be 2",
        "body": "Each choice is odd. Two odd primes add to an even number, so one of the primes must be 2. Then the other is the choice minus 2: $9, 15, 21, 29$. Only 29 is prime, so $31 = 2 + 29$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 31**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Check each",
        "body": "- $11 - 2 = 9 = 3 \\times 3$ ✗\n- $17 - 2 = 15 = 3 \\times 5$ ✗\n- $23 - 2 = 21 = 3 \\times 7$ ✗\n- $31 - 2 = 29$, prime ✓\n\n**Answer: (D) 31**"
      }
    ],
